    "q-105488": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105488",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $p(t)=5t$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t-1$ with respect to the inner product.",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{q(t)\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1)}{q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1)}\\cdot q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(5t){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{t=i}}{{\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(t-1){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t-1){|}_{t=i}}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5)\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 0}{(-2)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 0}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{5}\\cdot (t-1) \\\\  & =2(t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe distance between $p(t)=5t$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t-1$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖p(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-2(t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖3t+2‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨3t+2,3t+2⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨3t+2,3t+2⟩ & ={\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(3t+2){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (3t+2){|}_{t=i} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1+4+25 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{30}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
