      "source_example_id": "e-8733",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace",
      "kp_id": "e-8733"
    },
    "q-105510": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105510",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $2$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $p(t)=5{t}^{2}-5$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t+1$ with respect to the inner product.",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $p(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{q(t)\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t) & =\\frac{⟨p(t),q(t)⟩}{⟨q(t),q(t)⟩}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1)}{q(-1)q(-1)+q(0)q(0)+q(1)q(1)}\\cdot q(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(5{t}^{2}-5){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{t=i}}{{\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(t+1){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{t=i}}\\cdot (t+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 0+(-5)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 2}{0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2}\\cdot (t+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{-5}{5}\\cdot (t+1) \\\\  & =-t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe distance between $p(t)=5{t}^{2}-5$ and the subspace spanned by $q(t)=t+1$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖p(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{q(t)}\\,p(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖5{t}^{2}-5-(-t-1)‖ \\\\  & =‖5{t}^{2}+t-4‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨5{t}^{2}+t-4,5{t}^{2}+t-4⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5{t}^{2}+t-4,5{t}^{2}+t-4⟩ & ={\\sum }_{i\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}}(5{t}^{2}+t-4){|}_{t=i}\\cdot (5{t}^{2}+t-4){|}_{t=i} \\\\  & =(0)\\cdot (0)+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0+16+4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{20}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
